---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "August 31, 2026";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Canless Privacy Policy - bneuhausz.dev"
  description="Privacy policy for the Canless Android app."
  canonical="https://bneuhausz.dev/apps/canless/privacy/"
>
  <section
    class="prose dark:prose-invert text-left max-w-screen-md mx-auto px-8 pb-16"
  >
    <p class="text-sm text-amber-200/70">
      <a href="/apps/canless/">← Back to Canless</a>
    </p>

    <h1 class="text-3xl">Canless — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-amber-200/70">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Canless</strong> has no account and no server of ours. Everything
      you record in the app — your quit date, check-ins, cravings, slips and
      settings — is stored in a single file on your own device and is never
      uploaded by us. The third party involved is Google, through the ads,
      the purchases, and the crash reporting and usage statistics described
      below.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      The app is published by Bálint Neuhausz (Hungary), the data controller
      under the GDPR. Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@bneuhausz.dev"
        >contact@bneuhausz.dev</a
      >. Full business details are in the <a href="/imprint/">Imprint</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">Your data stays on your device</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Your whole progress is <strong>one file</strong> in the app's private
        storage. There is no cloud copy and no server that receives it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Export</strong> hands that file to you through the Android share
        sheet, and <strong>import</strong> reads a file you pick — both happen
        only when you ask, and the file goes only where you send it.
      </li>
      <li>
        The optional <strong>automatic backup</strong> (Premium) rewrites your
        save to a document <strong>you choose</strong> — for example a folder a
        cloud app of yours syncs. The app writes only to that one document you
        picked; where it syncs from there is between you and that app.
      </li>
      <li>
        There is no account and no login, so the app does not know who you
        are. What you log about your habit is never transmitted by us and is
        not shared with anyone.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
    <p>
      In the free version, a banner ad is served by <strong>Google AdMob</strong
      >. To show and measure ads, Google's advertising SDK may collect device
      and usage information, including your device's <strong
        >Advertising ID</strong
      >, device identifiers, approximate location derived from your IP
      address, and ad-interaction data. Google processes this as an
      independent controller under its own terms — see
      <a
        href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      In the European Economic Area, the UK, and Switzerland, the app shows a
      Google-certified <strong>consent prompt</strong> before personalized ads
      are used, so you can accept or decline. You can change your choice any
      time from <em>Settings → Ad privacy options</em> in the app. With
      Premium, the banner is not shown.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">Crash reports and usage statistics</h2>
    <p>
      The app uses <strong>Firebase Crashlytics</strong> to receive crash
      reports and <strong>Firebase Analytics</strong> for anonymous usage
      statistics (which screens and features are used, never the content of
      what you log — your check-ins, cravings and figures stay on the
      device). These services may process device identifiers and diagnostic
      information; Google's handling is described in
      <a
        href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">Purchases (Google Play Billing)</h2>
    <p>
      The Premium subscription, the one-off lifetime purchase and the shield
      packs are handled entirely by <strong>Google Play Billing</strong> — the
      app never sees your card or payment details, only whether a purchase is
      active.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">Notifications</h2>
    <p>
      The daily reminder and any extra nudges are <strong
        >scheduled locally on your device</strong
      >. There is no push service and nothing about them leaves your phone.
      They are off until you turn them on.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">Children</h2>
    <p>
      Canless is a general-audience app for people quitting energy drinks and
      is <strong>not directed at children under 13</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      There is no account for us to access or delete — uninstalling the app
      deletes its data from your device. Backup files you exported or set up
      yourself stay where you put them until you delete them. For the
      ad-related data Google collects, use the Google links above and your
      device's privacy controls. You can contact us at <a
        href="mailto:contact@bneuhausz.dev">contact@bneuhausz.dev</a
      >, and under the GDPR you may lodge a complaint with your local data
      protection authority.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl">Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, this page and the "last updated" date above will
      be updated.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
